 "summary": "Establishes the microenterprise development act to assist very small businesses and low-income business people.",
 "title": "Establishes the microenterprise development act to assist very small businesses and low-income business people",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A3767",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A3767-2017",
     "printNo": "A3767",
     "session": 2017,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 276\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 3767, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the economic development law, in relation to micro-\n      enterprise development\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill would amend the economic development law to establish a new\nmicroenterprise development grant program, which would provide funds for\norganizations to provide technical assistance for microenterprise entre-\npreneurs.\n \n  This bill would mandate at least  $1  million  annually  for  the  new\nprogram,  with  an initial investment of $1.5 million, an amount contem-\nplated outside of the budget process and  without  additional  appropri-\nations  for the funding. Further, this bill is duplicative of, and would\ncreate a competitor to, the existing Entrepreneurial Assistance  Program\n(EAP).  EAP  centers  currently receive around $1.7 million in the State\nBudget, and target the same community that  this  legislation  seeks  to\nassist,  serving clients who are 76% microbusinesses. For these reasons,\nI am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  This bill is disapproved.                   (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 276,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2018
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
